  "paragraph": "Odin asks for a hearing from a woman who remembers a world older than his own rule. She addresses the great and the small, the children of Heimdall, and looks past the god before her to the beginnings of everything. The voice is a seeress’s, but its movement is not a tidy history. Memory opens into vision; what has happened and what must happen stand close together. Odin wants knowledge, and she gives it to him without promising comfort.",
